                <pb facs="0632" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/1436: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Haitian Secretary of
                        State for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dejean</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">on Special Mission in the United States</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November 16,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Department received from American High Commissioner at Port-au-Prince a
                    telegram stating that President of Haiti desires following message, dated
                    November 14, received November 15, delivered to you: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Republic of Haiti is under no obligation to pay in gold either the
                            obligations of 1896 or those of 1910. Payment will be made in francs at
                            the rate of the day. Signed. Arthur Rameau, Secretary of State for
                            Justice.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
